403-5b24-9b80-21300bf72d36" :question/math-academy-id "q-93098" :question/problem "Find the root of $f(x)=-5\\sqrt[4]{3x+1}+10.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n-5\\sqrt[4]{3x+1}+10=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\sqrt[4]{3x+1}+10 & =0 \\\\ -5\\sqrt[4]{3x+1} & =-10 \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{3x+1} & =2 \\\\ (\\sqrt[4]{3x+1})^{4} & ={2}^{4} \\\\ 3x+1 & =16 \\\\ 3x & =15 \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we must check the answer by substituting it back into the initial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\sqrt[4]{3\\cdot 5+1}+10 & =0 \\\\ -5\\sqrt[4]{16}+10 & =0 \\\\ -5\\cdot 2+10 & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-93098/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d059c56-ae7f-5fb6-8bc6-2ce97bb7f876"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93098"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93099/selection/8a9795ac20a315e2300611ae90ca9198f52a4692b8e3e236c32bc3b963d97863" :answer/id #uuid "085dc9a7-a9f8-5485-86b1-5d90a75620e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93099/selection/b0a6c2ce27d12795e2cb0f5cdfa9bfdcf9b444e8dc861be04be7982e5d533c0b" :answer/id #uuid "fc819e07-765c-5334-9dcd-6dc57ced0953" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The function has no root" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93099/selection/e9cc9fbdbc5a650d2ee650950a0b51e4a2918a2768c2af7243cea1a77ce42b70" :answer/id #uuid "d2323aef-800c-5cf2-9654-6e3a8b2bfb76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93099/selection/bcd5759b2ef11af8235b2991e5d920cd9c3f5d9d26eb743b9ec76ea5e99b553c" :answer/id #uuid "aa94f550-247e-5e25-9f74-77e244b33b04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm 13" :db/ensure [